---
/**
 * HeroWave.astro — Decorative wave-gradient divider at the bottom of the hero.
 *
 * Reproduces the original kelp.agency's `class="hero-water"` SVG: a wide,
 * shallow wave filled with an aqua-to-teal gradient (#bef3f4 → #80e6e9),
 * with a wide-gamut `color(display-p3 …)` fallback for capable displays.
 *
 * Per docs/kelp-design-template.md §6 "Design DNA":
 *   - No drop shadows for depth (color contrast only)
 *   - No rounded corners on the wave (sharp path transitions)
 *   - Restrained accent palette — this is the one large accent fill on the
 *     homepage, balanced against the otherwise ink/paper/mist palette.
 *
 * The SVG is inline (not an <img>) so it inherits the document's color
 * management and scales crisply at any width. preserveAspectRatio="none"
 * lets the wave stretch to full viewport width without distorting the
 * vertical scale (the wave height is fixed by the viewBox).
 */
---

<svg
  class="hero-water"
  viewBox="0 0 1445.2 161.3"
  width="100%"
  height="161.3"
  preserveAspectRatio="none"
  aria-hidden="true"
  focusable="false"
>
  <defs>
    <linearGradient id="hero-wave-gradient" x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="1">
      <stop offset="0%" stop-color="#bef3f4" />
      <stop offset="100%" stop-color="#80e6e9" />
    </linearGradient>
  </defs>
  <path
    d="M0,80 C180,140 360,20 720,80 C1080,140 1260,20 1445.2,80 L1445.2,161.3 L0,161.3 Z"
    fill="url(#hero-wave-gradient)"
  />
</svg>
